ITEMS = ((('when should i start cpr on a child', 'what are the signs that a child needs cpr', 'how do i know when to begin child cpr', 'when is cpr needed for a young child', 'what if a child is not breathing normally', 'how to decide about cpr for a child', 'when to begin chest compressions on children', 'what condition requires cpr in a child', 'how do i recognise a cardiac arrest in a child', 'when should a bystander start cpr for a child'), "Start CPR if a child is unresponsive and not breathing normally. Call emergency services first or send someone to call, then begin compressions and rescue breaths if you are trained. A child's arrest often follows breathing problems, so tell the operator what happened."), (('how do i check if a child needs cpr', 'how long should i check breathing before child cpr', 'should i check a pulse before cpr for a child', 'how to shake and shout at an unresponsive child', 'what to look for before starting cpr on a child', 'how to tell if a child is breathing normally during child cpr', 'should i tilt the head before child cpr', 'how to check response in a collapsed child', "what if i am unsure about a child's breathing", 'how to assess a child before starting cpr'), 'Check if the child responds and look for normal breathing. If there is no response and no normal breath, begin CPR without delay. If you are not trained in finding a pulse, do not spend time trying, and call emergency services.'), (('how do i do chest compressions on a child', 'where do i push for child cpr', 'how deep should chest compressions be for a child', 'how fast should i do cpr on a child', 'what is the correct hand position for child cpr', 'should i use one hand for child compressions', 'how to keep compressions going for children', 'what does good child cpr feel like', 'can i do cpr alone on a child', 'how to avoid tiring during child compressions'), 'For a child, push on the centre of the chest with one hand or two as needed for their size, firmly and evenly. Let the chest rise between compressions and keep pauses short. Call emergency services and continue until a qualified person takes over.'), (('should i give rescue breaths during child cpr', 'how do i give rescue breaths to a child', 'what is the ratio of breaths to compressions for children', 'can i do cpr without breaths on a child', 'how to open the airway for child rescue breaths', 'is mouth to mouth needed for child cpr', 'what if i am not trained in rescue breaths for children', 'how long should a rescue breath be for a child', 'can a barrier device help with child cpr', 'when to use compression only cpr on children'), "Rescue breaths are especially valuable in child CPR, so give them if you are trained and willing. If you cannot, use continuous compressions instead. Call emergency services and follow the operator's guidance rather than stopping altogether."), (('how do i do cpr on a baby or toddler', 'is child cpr different for a toddler', 'how to adapt cpr for a small child', 'what size of hand for infant compressions during child cpr', 'how to do rescue breaths on a toddler during child cpr', 'can i use adult technique for a young child', 'what changes in cpr as a child grows', 'how to support a tiny body during cpr', 'when to learn infant cpr properly', 'who can teach cpr for babies and children'), 'CPR technique changes with the size of the child, using gentler pressure and smaller breaths for a baby or toddler. The safest approach is to practise on a course with a qualified instructor. Call emergency services and follow their instructions in an emergency.'), (('how long should i continue cpr on a child', 'when is it ok to stop child cpr', 'what if the child starts breathing during cpr', 'should i keep doing cpr until the ambulance arrives during child cpr', 'how to know if child cpr is working', 'what if i am too tired to continue child cpr', 'when to hand over cpr of a child to another person', 'how long can bystanders do cpr for a child', 'what to do if the child wakes up', 'who can tell me to stop cpr on a child'), 'Continue CPR until the child shows signs of life, you cannot go on, or a qualified person tells you to stop. If normal breathing returns, stop compressions and hold the child in a safe position while waiting. Stay close and keep watching their breathing.'), (('how do two people do cpr on a child', 'should i swap over during child cpr', 'what is the best handover for child compressions', 'can a bystander help with cpr for a child', 'how to direct helpers during child cpr', 'what if two trained people arrive for a child', 'how often should rescuers change during child cpr', 'how to coordinate breaths and compressions in children', 'what to say to someone assisting with child cpr', 'when to ask a bystander to take over child cpr'), 'Two responders can share child CPR, with one doing compressions and the other giving breaths if trained. Swap before you become tired and keep interruptions brief. Emergency services can talk you through it until their crew arrives.'), (('should i do cpr after a child is choking', 'how to start cpr following child choking', 'what if a child collapses after choking', 'can cpr help a child after near drowning', 'is cpr needed after a child electric shock', 'how to begin cpr after a child fall', 'what to do before cpr for a sick child', 'how to warm a child during cpr', 'when to get help with cpr after an incident', 'what to tell the operator before child cpr'), 'If a child collapses after choking or near drowning, call emergency services and start CPR when they are not breathing normally. Clear only a visible object from the mouth. Tell the operator the cause, as it may affect the advice they give.'), (('what position should a child be in for cpr', 'should i move a child before starting cpr', 'how to place a child flat for compressions', 'is cpr safe if a child fell from height', 'what if the child is on a bed when cpr is needed', 'how to protect the airway during child cpr', "should i lift a child's legs during cpr", 'what if the floor is cold during child cpr', 'how to roll a child for cpr', 'when to avoid moving a child before cpr'), 'Place the child on their back on a firm surface if possible, keeping them warm without delaying compressions. If a fall or spinal injury is possible, move them as little as you can. Call emergency services and ask for advice while you begin.'), (("does cpr restart a child's heart", 'what are the chances of recovery with child cpr', 'should i try cpr if the child looks pale', 'can cpr harm a child who is not in arrest', 'what if i am unsure whether to start child cpr', 'is it better to attempt cpr than do nothing during child cpr', 'how quickly must cpr start in children', 'what to expect after child cpr', 'who decides when child cpr is finished', 'when to call emergency services before child cpr'), "CPR may keep oxygen reaching a child's brain until emergency help arrives, though it cannot always reverse the cause. If you are unsure, call emergency services and begin compressions. A qualified team will take over and decide about further treatment."))
